  "body": "#706 has merged into upstream main; this PR is no longer stacked and targets `main` with only its own files. Main's `crates/app/src/pick/roles.rs` already carries the `(Role::Z, Role::Y)` arm fix below (identical hunk, taken from main in the merge). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New MCP tool `set_wcs_from_features`** (`crates/app/src/mcp/wcs_tools.rs`): picks are `[{model, id, role}]`, `role` one of `origin | x | y | z`, ids from `list_features`. It runs the GUI's own law `pick::align_roles` (#701) unchanged, turns the fit into a WCS placement exactly as the GUI's `CommandKind::SetWcs` does (`quat_from_euler` of the law's roll/pitch/yaw), and executes the existing undoable `SetWcsOrigin` - no new command kind, no frame maths of its own, one undo step. Picks go through the same id parse, model check and one-pick rule (#692) as every other MCP pick. Optional `setup` must name the active setup (`SetWcsOrigin` places the active setup's WCS; the GUI greys Apply on an inactive row the same way) - otherwise refused by name. The reply carries the placed origin/rotation/word plus the fitted `axes` and `angles_deg`.\n- **Fix to the law, `(Z, Y)` role pair** (`crates/app/src/pick/roles.rs`): with a Z pick and a Y pick (no X), `align_roles` put the Z pick's axis in the Y slot and the Y pick in X - the arm was a copy of `(Y, X)`. A box with Z = its +X side face and Y = that side's top edge came out x = [0,1,0], y = [1,0,0], z = [0,0,-1]: a WCS lying on its back, posting turned moves. Now Z stays Z, Y is squared to it, X = Y x Z. Now on main via #706 (identical hunk); this PR no longer changes `roles.rs`.\n- camcraft-mcp skill: tool row, shipped-gaps line, and a caveat that a `list_features` face row's `normal` is the canonical plane normal (#956). `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 33 -> 36 (#681 entry to be posted at merge: `PROCESS_VERSION 36` · PR #960 · camcraft-mcp skill gains the `set_wcs_from_features` row · forks: sync process files).\n- `docs/decisions/937-mcp-wcs-from-features.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/mcp_wcs_features.rs` (gate map: app::mcp::wcs_tools, app::pick::roles):\n- `set_wcs_from_features_lands_on_the_guis_frame_as_one_undo_step` - three pick sets (plain 3-2-1; Z face + Y edge + corner; Z face + X edge + a cylinder wall patch as origin) on a box and a 48-segment bore imported over MCP. For each, the placed origin and rotation equal **bit for bit** what `align_roles` plus the GUI's `quat_from_euler` conversion give on an identical in-process world; the frames are then spelled out (identity at the corner; Z on the side's normal, Y along the edge, X = Y x Z; the bore's fitted centre projected onto the top face). Undo/redo walk one step each. **Red on `d2663a3f` without the roles fix, green with it.**\n- `bad_feature_picks_are_refused_by_name_and_place_nothing` - missing `picks`, empty and single pick, a role given twice, fewer than two axes, a vertex as an axis, an edge as the origin, parallel axes (top face Z + vertical edge X), a stale id, a bad role word, an unknown model, an extra pick key, an inactive `setup`, an unknown argument; the WCS stays unplaced.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green at `be055d7d` - app suites (31 binaries incl. `mcp_wcs_features`, `wcs_roles`, `mcp_setup`, `mcp_pick`) ok in 33 s, ui suites (lib + 10 binaries) ok in 124 s; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The live-GUI path (`--mcp-port`) - the tool runs on the same `Env`/History as every other tool, nothing GUI-specific.\n- A UI test for the GUI row with a Z+Y pair - the fix is in the shared law; the GUI row calls the same function.\n- No script verb: `set_wcs` has none either.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- #956 - `list_features` reports a face's canonical plane normal, not its outward side (an agent steered by `normal`/`facing` picks the wrong face).\n\nChangelog: MCP `set_wcs_from_features` places the active setup's WCS from feature picks with origin/x/y/z roles, through the GUI's \"Set WCS from features\" law and the same undoable command; a Z pick with a Y pick now keeps Z on Z (it landed on Y) (#937)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #937\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n\nMerge order with the other process PRs: #1161 (34), #1309 (35), then this (36).\n",
